## How it works

| Feature | Technique |
|---|---|
| **Responsive columns** | Mobile-first CSS Grid: `1fr` by default, `repeat(2, 1fr)` at 640px, `repeat(3, 1fr)` at 1024px |
| **Equal-height cards** | Grid stretches items by default; `flex-grow: 1` on `.product-info` and `.product-description` pushes the price/button row to the bottom so footers line up |
| **Consistent images** | `aspect-ratio: 3 / 2` + `object-fit: cover` crops images uniformly without distortion |
| **Interactivity** | Subtle lift and image zoom on hover; visible focus ring for keyboard users |
| **Accessibility** | Semantic `<article>` elements, descriptive `alt` text, and `:focus-visible` styling |

**Optional alternative:** If you'd rather not use breakpoints, you can replace the grid rules with:

```css
.product-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr));
  gap: 2rem;
}
```

This auto-fits as many columns as space allows. With the 1200px container, that results in 3 columns on desktop and 1 on mobile, but the media-query version gives you more precise control.

