  background-color: var(--color-primary);
  border: none;
  border-radius: 8px;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
}

.btn:hover {
  background-color: var(--color-primary-hover);
}

.btn:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid #93c5fd;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

/* Respect reduced-motion preferences */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .product-card,
  .product-image img {
    transition: none;
  }
  .product-card:hover,
  .product-card:hover .product-image img {
    transform: none;
  }
}
```

## How it works

| Screen width | Columns | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| < 600px (mobile) | 1 | `grid-template-columns: 1fr` |
| 600–959px (tablet) | 2 | `repeat(2, 1fr)` |
| ≥ 960px (desktop) | 3 | `repeat(3, 1fr)` |

**Key techniques:**
- **Mobile-first CSS Grid.** The base style is one column, and `min-width` media queries add columns as the screen grows.
- **Equal-height cards.** Grid stretches the cards in each row, and `flex: 1` on `.product-body` with `margin-top: auto` on the footer keeps prices and buttons aligned at the bottom.
- **Consistent images.** `aspect-ratio: 3/2` with `object-fit: cover` keeps every image the same shape without distortion.
- **Accessibility.** The grid uses a semantic list (`<ul>`/`<li>`), images have alt text, buttons have a visible focus state, and animations are disabled for users who prefer reduced motion.

If you only want the two breakpoints you asked for (1 column on mobile, 3 on desktop), delete the 600px media query.

