## How It Works

| Screen width | Columns | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| `< 600px` (mobile) | 1 | Default `grid-template-columns: 1fr` |
| `600px – 991px` (tablet) | 2 | `@media (min-width: 600px)` |
| `≥ 992px` (desktop) | 3 | `@media (min-width: 992px)` |

**Key techniques:**
- **Mobile-first**: The base style is a single column; media queries add columns as the screen grows.
- **Equal-height cards**: Each card is a flex column, and `flex-grow: 1` on the description pushes the price/button footer to the bottom, so buttons line up even when descriptions vary in length.
- **Consistent images**: `aspect-ratio: 3 / 2` with `object-fit: cover` keeps all images the same shape without distortion.
- **Accessibility**: Semantic `<article>` elements, `alt` text on images, and a visible `:focus-visible` outline on buttons.

**Want strictly 3 → 1 with no tablet step?** Remove the 600px media query block.

