## How It Works

| Screen width | Columns | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| < 600px (mobile) | 1 | Default `grid-template-columns: 1fr` |
| 600px – 959px (tablet) | 2 | `repeat(2, 1fr)` |
| ≥ 960px (desktop) | 3 | `repeat(3, 1fr)` |

**Key techniques:**
- **Mobile-first** – base styles target small screens, and `min-width` media queries add columns as space allows.
- **`aspect-ratio` + `object-fit: cover`** – keeps all images a uniform size regardless of the source dimensions.
- **Flexbox inside cards** – `flex-grow: 1` on the description pushes the price/button row to the bottom, so footers line up even when descriptions vary in length.
- **Semantic markup** – `<article>` for each card, `<del>` for the old price, and `alt` text on images for accessibility.

If you'd rather skip the tablet breakpoint and go straight from 1 to 3 columns, just delete the `@media (min-width: 600px)` block.

