## How It Works

| Screen width | Columns | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| `< 640px` (mobile) | 1 | Default `grid-template-columns: 1fr` |
| `640px – 1023px` (tablet) | 2 | `repeat(2, 1fr)` |
| `≥ 1024px` (desktop) | 3 | `repeat(3, 1fr)` |

**Key techniques:**
- **Mobile-first approach**: The base styles target mobile, and `min-width` media queries layer on larger layouts.
- **Equal-height cards**: Grid stretches items in a row to the same height. `flex: 1` on `.product-description` pushes the price/button footer to the bottom, so footers align even when descriptions differ in length.
- **Consistent images**: `aspect-ratio: 3 / 2` with `object-fit: cover` keeps images uniform without distortion.
- **Accessibility**: Semantic `<article>` elements, descriptive `alt` text, and a visible `:focus-visible` state on buttons.

> 💡 **Strict 3/1 only?** If you want to skip the tablet step, delete the `640px` media query. Cards will then stay at 1 column until 1024px.

