## How it keeps thumbnails even

| Technique | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr))` | Creates equal-width columns that wrap responsively, with no media queries needed |
| `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` | Forces every thumbnail container to be a perfect square |
| `object-fit: cover` | Fills the square by cropping instead of stretching, so mixed portrait and landscape images all look uniform |
| `width: 100%; height: 100%` on `img` | Makes the image fill its container exactly |

## Easy customizations

- **Different shape:** Change `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` to `4 / 3` or `16 / 9` for rectangular thumbnails.
- **Bigger or smaller thumbnails:** Adjust the `220px` in `minmax(220px, 1fr)`.
- **Spacing:** Change the `gap` value.
- **Your own photos:** Replace the `picsum.photos` URLs with your image paths. The `href` can point to the full-size version.

