## How the even sizing works

| Technique | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr))` | Creates as many equal-width columns as fit, resizing responsively |
| `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` | Gives every thumbnail the same height as its width (change to `4 / 3` or `16 / 9` if preferred) |
| `object-fit: cover` | Crops images to fill the box without stretching, so mixed portrait/landscape photos look uniform |

## Customization tips

- **Change thumbnail size:** adjust `--thumb-min` in `:root`.
- **Change shape:** swap `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` for `4 / 3`, `3 / 2`, etc.
- **Fixed column count:** replace the grid rule with `repeat(4, 1fr)`.
- **Use your own photos:** replace the `src` (thumbnail) and `href` (full-size) URLs, and update the `alt` text to describe each image.

