## How the even sizing works

| Technique | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr))` | Fits as many columns as possible. Each column is at least 220px wide, and all columns stretch equally to fill the row. |
| `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` | Makes every tile's height match its width, so all thumbnails are identical squares. |
| `object-fit: cover` | Scales each image to fill its tile and crops the overflow. Portrait and landscape photos never distort or leave gaps. |
| `overflow: hidden` | Clips the image when it scales up on hover. |

## Customization tips

- **Rectangular thumbnails:** change `aspect-ratio` to `4 / 3` or `16 / 9`.
- **Larger or smaller tiles:** adjust the `220px` value in `minmax()`.
- **Fixed column count:** replace the grid rule with `repeat(4, 1fr)`.
- **Your own photos:** swap the `picsum.photos` URLs. Point the `<img src>` at a thumbnail and the `<a href>` at the full-size image.

