## How the even sizing works

Three CSS properties do the heavy lifting:

1. **`grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr))`**: creates as many equal-width columns as will fit, each at least 220px wide. Columns reflow automatically as the screen resizes, without media queries.

2. **`aspect-ratio: 1 / 1`**: gives every thumbnail container the same height as its width, so all tiles are identical squares.

3. **`object-fit: cover`**: makes each image fill its square completely, cropping the excess instead of stretching. Portrait, landscape, and square photos all look uniform. (The sample images deliberately use mixed dimensions to show this.)

## Customization tips

- **Different shape:** change `aspect-ratio` to `4 / 3` or `16 / 9` for rectangular thumbnails.
- **Bigger or smaller tiles:** adjust the `220px` value in `minmax()`.
- **Spacing:** tweak the `gap` value.
- **Crop focus:** add `object-position: top;` (or `center`, `left`, etc.) to control which part of the image stays visible.
- **Your own photos:** replace the `picsum.photos` URLs with your image paths. Ideally, use small thumbnail files in the grid and full-size files in the lightbox for faster loading.

