### How the Gallery Stays Even

The layout uses a few key CSS techniques to keep every thumbnail identical in size, no matter the original image dimensions.

- **Uniform square tiles** — Each thumbnail link has `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1`, so every tile is a perfect square. The grid columns use `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr))`, which stretches each column to fill the row evenly.
- **Image cropping without distortion** — Images use `object-fit: cover` and `object-position: center`, so they fill the square by cropping rather than stretching. This keeps the grid tidy even when source photos have different aspect ratios.
- **Responsive and accessible** — The grid automatically adjusts the number of columns based on screen width. Hover and focus states add a subtle lift and zoom, while `prefers-reduced-motion` disables those animations for users who prefer less motion.
