### How the Gallery Works

The page uses a responsive grid and a few CSS tricks to keep every thumbnail the same size, no matter the original image dimensions.

- **Even thumbnails:** Each gallery item has `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1`, making every tile a perfect square. The images use `object-fit: cover`, so they crop to fill the square without stretching or distorting.
- **Responsive grid:** The grid uses `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr))`, so it automatically fits as many columns as the screen allows. On smaller screens, the minimum column width drops to 140px.
- **Hover and focus feedback:** Hovering over a tile lifts it slightly and zooms the image inside. Keyboard users get the same effect when focusing the link, plus a visible focus outline.
- **Accessibility touches:** Images include descriptive `alt` text, lazy loading is enabled, and the `prefers-reduced-motion` media query disables animations for users who prefer less motion.
---

**Optimization Tip:** You can replace the `picsum.photos` image URLs with your own photo paths, and adjust the `minmax(200px, 1fr)` value to change the thumbnail size.

