### Uniform Thumbnails & Hover Interactions

The page uses a responsive grid to keep every thumbnail the same size, no matter the original image dimensions.

- **Responsive grid** — `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(220px, 100%), 1fr))` creates as many columns as fit, with each tile at least 220px wide. This keeps the layout even on screens from mobile to desktop.
- **Fixed aspect ratio** — Each `.thumb` uses `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1`, so every tile is a perfect square regardless of the source image's shape.
- **Cropping with `object-fit`** — Images fill the square via `object-fit: cover`, so they won't stretch or distort. The image stays centered and any overflow is cropped.
- **Hover and focus feedback** — Hovering a thumbnail scales the image slightly and dims it, while the caption slides up from the bottom. Keyboard users can tab to each tile and see the same effects.
- **Motion and accessibility** — A `prefers-reduced-motion` media query disables transitions for users who prefer less motion, and a visible focus outline helps keyboard navigation.
