### Pricing Card Layout & Interaction

This pricing section keeps the focus on clarity and quick comparison across the three plans.

- **Three equal-width cards** sit side by side on desktop, each with a plan name, short description, price, call-to-action button, and a feature list.
- **The middle “Pro” card is visually highlighted** with a colored border, a “Most popular” badge, and a filled primary button to draw attention.
- **Hover feedback** lifts each card slightly and deepens its shadow, while buttons change background color on hover and show a focus ring for keyboard users.
- **Responsive stacking** switches the layout to a single column on smaller screens, and the featured plan is reordered to the top so it’s seen first.
- **Reduced motion support** disables transitions and hover lift for users who prefer less animation.
---

**Optimization Tip:** You can replace the plan names, prices, feature lists, and button link destinations (`href="#"`) with your own content. The brand color is controlled by the `--accent` CSS variable, so updating it will recolor the highlighted card, badge, and checkmarks automatically.

