**Key points**

- `display: grid` with `grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr)` gives exactly three equal-width columns on desktop.
- Media queries step the layout down: 2 columns below `900px`, 1 column below `600px`.
- `aspect-ratio: 4 / 3` + `object-fit: cover` keeps every image the same size regardless of source dimensions.
- `flex: 1` on `.card-description` pushes the price/button row to the bottom, so cards align even when text lengths differ.
- The `max-width: 1200px` container keeps the grid readable on very wide screens.

**Alternative (auto-fit) if you don't need a fixed 3-column count:**

```css
.product-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
  gap: 1.5rem;
}
```

This fills each row with as many ~280px cards as fit — 3 on desktop, 1 on phones — without any media queries.

