```js
// gallery.js — optional category filtering
const buttons = document.querySelectorAll('.filter');
const photos  = document.querySelectorAll('.photo');
const empty   = document.getElementById('empty');

buttons.forEach(btn => {
  btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    buttons.forEach(b => b.classList.remove('is-active'));
    btn.classList.add('is-active');

    const filter = btn.dataset.filter;
    let visible = 0;

    photos.forEach(photo => {
      const show = filter === 'all' || photo.dataset.category === filter;
      photo.classList.toggle('is-hidden', !show);
      if (show) visible++;
    });

    empty.hidden = visible !== 0;
  });
});
```

### Key techniques for evenly sized thumbnails

| Technique | Why it matters |
|---|---|
| `display: grid` + `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr))` | Columns are fluid and equal width; rows align automatically. |
| `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` on `.photo` | Every cell is a perfect square, independent of image dimensions. |
| `object-fit: cover` on `img` | Fills the square and crops the overflow evenly instead of stretching. |
| `overflow: hidden` + `border-radius` | Clean rounded corners on the cropped image. |
| `loading="lazy"` | Keeps the page fast with many photos. |

**Variations:** change `aspect-ratio` to `4 / 3` or `16 / 9` for landscape tiles; use `grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr)` for a fixed 4-across layout; add `grid-auto-rows` + `grid-auto-flow: dense` if you want a masonry-like fill.

