## Key techniques for evenly sized thumbnails

| Technique | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `display: grid` + `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr))` | Responsive columns that reflow automatically |
| `aspect-ratio: 4 / 3` on the tile | Forces every tile to the identical height/width ratio |
| `object-fit: cover` on the `<img>` | Crops images to fill the tile without distortion |
| `width/height: 100%` + `display: block` | Removes inline-image gaps and fills the tile |
| `overflow: hidden` + `border-radius` | Clips the zoom effect to rounded corners |
| `loading="lazy"` | Defers off-screen image loading for speed |

**To use square thumbnails instead**, change `aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;` to `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;`.

**To use your own photos**, replace the `src` values with your image paths — the sizing stays uniform no matter the original image dimensions.

