## How the "evenly sized thumbnails" work

| Technique | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `display: grid` + `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr))` | Columns are equal width and auto-wrap responsively. |
| `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` on the link | Every frame is exactly the same height, no matter the image's original ratio. |
| `object-fit: cover` on the image | Fills the square frame while cropping the overflow evenly (no distortion). |
| `object-position: center` | Controls which part stays visible when cropping. |
| `overflow: hidden` + `border-radius` | Clips the zoomed image to the rounded frame. |

### Optional variations

**Uniform rectangles instead of squares** — change to `aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;` (or `16 / 9`).

**Fixed column count** — replace the `auto-fill` track with `repeat(4, 1fr)` and add a media query for smaller screens.

**Masonry-style (variable heights)** — use `grid-template-rows: masonry` (limited support) or a JS column-balancing script; note this breaks the "evenly sized" requirement.

**No-JS lightbox alternative** — the `:target` trick above is pure CSS; if you'd rather use JavaScript, swap the anchors for `<button>` elements and toggle a class.

