## How the "evenly sized" part works

| Technique | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `display: grid` + `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr))` | Columns are equal width and wrap responsively — no column-count media queries needed. |
| `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` on `.gallery-item` | Forces every thumbnail box to the same shape regardless of the source image's dimensions. Change to `4 / 3` or `3 / 2` for landscape tiles. |
| `object-fit: cover` on `img` | Fills the box and crops the overflow instead of distorting the image. |
| `width/height: 100%` on `img` | Lets the image fill its grid cell completely. |

### Variations you might want

**Fixed number of columns instead of auto-fill:**
```css
.gallery {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
}
@media (max-width: 900px) { .gallery { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
@media (max-width: 600px) { .gallery { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
```

**Masonry-style (variable heights, still equal widths):**
```css
.gallery { columns: 4 220px; column-gap: 18px; }
.gallery-item { break-inside: avoid; margin-bottom: 18px; }
```

**Prevent layout shift while images load** — add `width` and `height` attributes to your `<img>` tags matching their intrinsic ratio, e.g. `width="600" height="600"`.

**Using your own images** — just replace the `src` URLs; the grid handles any image size automatically.

