## `script.js` (optional lightbox)

```js
document.querySelectorAll('.thumb').forEach(link => {
  link.addEventListener('click', e => {
    e.preventDefault();
    const box = document.createElement('div');
    box.className = 'lightbox';
    box.innerHTML = `
      <a href="#" class="lightbox__close" aria-label="Close">&times;</a>
      <img src="${link.getAttribute('href')}" alt="${link.querySelector('img').alt}">`;
    document.body.appendChild(box);

    const close = () => box.remove();
    box.addEventListener('click', e => { if (e.target === box || e.target.classList.contains('lightbox__close')) close(); });
    document.addEventListener('keydown', function esc(e) {
      if (e.key === 'Escape') { close(); document.removeEventListener('keydown', esc); }
    });
  });
});
```

### Key techniques for evenly sized thumbnails

| Technique | Why it matters |
|---|---|
| `display: grid` + `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr))` | Columns are all equal width and wrap responsively without media queries. |
| `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` on the tile | Locks the height so every tile is a perfect square regardless of image dimensions. |
| `object-fit: cover` on the `<img>` | Fills the square and crops overflow instead of distorting the photo. |
| `width/height: 100%` on the image | Stretches the image to the tile box for `object-fit` to work. |
| `aspect-ratio` on the tile (not the img) | Reserves space before the image loads, preventing layout shift. |

**To use your own photos:** drop the files in a `photos/` folder and change both the `href` (full-size) and `src` (thumbnail) paths. For local files, the thumbnail can point to the same image — `object-fit: cover` will crop it to a square automatically.

